CAT = "phnleProf"; SEG = "PRO"
# Professional nursing practice integrated across the parts: R.A. 9173, the Code of Ethics for
# Registered Nurses, legal and ethical principles, leadership and management. 12 items, 3 per test.
Q = [
("Under the Philippine Nursing Act of 2002 (R.A. 9173), the Professional Regulatory Board of Nursing is composed of:",
 "A chairperson and six members", ["A chairperson and four members", "Nine elected members", "A chairperson and two members"],
 "Section 3 of R.A. 9173 provides for a chairperson and six members, appointed by the President from nominees of the accredited professional organization."),
("A registered nurse has not practiced for five consecutive years and wants to return to work. Under R.A. 9173 she must first:",
 "Complete a refresher program", ["Retake the licensure exam", "Apply for a new license number", "Work one year as an aide"],
 "Section 26 requires nurses inactive for five consecutive years to complete one month of didactic training and three months of practicum."),
("Under R.A. 9173, suturing of a perineal laceration by a nurse is allowed only:",
 "After special training", ["With the patient's verbal request", "When no midwife is present", "In a private clinic"],
 "Section 28 lists internal examination during labor and delivery among a nurse's duties and adds that, for suturing of perineal laceration, special training shall be provided according to established protocol."),
("A nurse tells a patient that a painful injection will not hurt at all. Which ethical principle does this violate?",
 "Veracity", ["Fidelity", "Justice", "Autonomy"],
 "Veracity is the duty to tell the truth. Fidelity is keeping promises; justice is fair distribution of care."),
("A competent adult with diabetes refuses an amputation after a full explanation. The nurse respects the refusal. This upholds:",
 "Autonomy", ["Beneficence", "Paternalism", "Nonmaleficence"],
 "Autonomy is a competent person's right to decide about their own care, including refusing treatment after informed consent is given."),
("A nurse gives 10 units of insulin instead of the ordered 1 unit, and the patient becomes hypoglycemic. The nurse's liability rests on:",
 "Negligence", ["Battery", "Defamation", "Assault"],
 "Malpractice by a professional needs a duty, a breach of the standard of care, injury, and the breach causing the injury. All four are present."),
("A nurse restrains an alert, oriented adult who wants to leave against medical advice, without any order. This may be:",
 "False imprisonment", ["Assault", "Invasion of privacy", "Slander"],
 "Unjustified restraint of a person's movement is false imprisonment. A competent adult may leave against advice after signing the hospital's waiver."),
("Who is responsible for explaining the risks of a surgical procedure when obtaining informed consent?",
 "The surgeon", ["The staff nurse", "The anesthesiologist only", "The nursing supervisor"],
 "The physician performing the procedure explains it, its risks and alternatives. The nurse may witness the signature and confirms the patient understands."),
("A head nurse makes all unit decisions alone and expects staff to follow without discussion. This leadership style is:",
 "Autocratic", ["Democratic", "Laissez-faire", "Situational"],
 "An autocratic leader decides alone and directs others. It suits emergencies but lowers morale in routine work."),
("In which care delivery model does one registered nurse hold 24-hour responsibility for a patient's care from admission to discharge?",
 "Primary nursing", ["Team nursing", "Functional nursing", "Case method by shift"],
 "In primary nursing one nurse plans and is accountable for the patient's care around the clock. Functional nursing assigns tasks, not patients."),
("A nurse posts a photo of a patient's wound on social media without a name. Under the Data Privacy Act (R.A. 10173), this is:",
 "A breach of confidentiality", ["Allowed if the face is hidden", "Allowed for teaching", "A matter of hospital etiquette only"],
 "Health information is sensitive personal information under R.A. 10173. Sharing it without consent, even unnamed, breaches privacy and the Code of Ethics."),
("Under R.A. 10912, a Philippine registered nurse renews the professional license after completing:",
 "Required CPD units", ["A new licensure exam", "A hospital service year", "A master's degree"],
 "The Continuing Professional Development Act of 2016 links license renewal to CPD units in learning activities accredited by the CPD Council."),
]
